  "term": "hippocampal formation",
  "definition": "The hippocampal formation is a brain structure examined in relation to cognition, especially learning, memory, and brain cell development. In this packet, it is described as an area where offspring showed higher BDNF levels and greater numbers of neuronal and non-neuronal cells alongside better performance on memory-related tasks.",
